        "essence_text": "A jagged, caffeinated plunge into late-90s male alienation that treats consumer comfort as a kind of spiritual death. The film’s swaggering voice and sardonic wit make nihilism feel electric, then yank the floor out from under you. Fights land as both spectacle and confession, a brutal ritual against a world of IKEA catalogs and office cubicles. Stylish, talky, and meanly funny, it rewards rewatches as much for its structural trickery as for its lingering unease. You leave buzzing, implicated, and a little raw."
